    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `timezone` field to the owner response, derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Regions.java`** \u2014 Added a pinned `REGION_TIMEZONE` map (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `timezoneOf(String region)` lookup returning the IANA name (or `null` for regions with no pinned timezone, e.g. `UNKNOWN`).\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `timezone` mapping that derives the region the same way `locality` does (`CustomerCode.region(...)`) and resolves it through `Regions.timezoneOf(...)`, keeping both fields consistent.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `timezone` string property to the owner schema (the `OwnerDto` is generated from this at build time).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` passes: a Sydney owner (postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW) now reports `locality: NSW` and `timezone: Australia/Sydney`. **BUILD SUCCESS**, 1 test run, 0 failures.",
