    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing structure:\n\n- `Regions` is already the established home for region-keyed lookup tables (`CITY_REGION`, `REGION_POSTCODES`). Adding `REGION_TIMEZONE` as a third `Map.of` table plus a `timezoneOf(region)` accessor follows the exact pattern already present \u2014 same declaration style, same null-when-absent contract, same Javadoc tone. It is not making the class a catch-all; it's precisely the kind of region-derivation lookup this class exists for.\n- The new mapper `@Mapping` mirrors the adjacent `locality` mapping and composes the existing `CustomerCode.region(...)` output as the region input, rather than re-deriving anything \u2014 no duplication of the region logic.\n- The OpenAPI `timezone` property is placed next to `locality` with a description consistent with its siblings.\n\nLogic lives in the right unit (the lookup table in `Regions`, not inlined into the mapper expression or duplicated), and a maintainer would find this the natural place to add it.",
